    "quotes_YaCamG": {
      "type": "quotes",
      "blocks": {
        "quote_7Xw8cU": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Durable & One-of-a-kind",
            "author": "Roy Y",
            "info": "",
            "date": "Aug 2nd",
            "rate": 5,
            "quote": "I don't even have a clue how many shots mine has through it but in the 4 digits. It has been shot with 22s, 9mm, 40S&W, 10mm, 45s of various descriptions and is still working. The only open holes are about 1/4\" where we intentionally shot it with some 45 WFNs. If you hit those holes with a 9mm it will still contact the edges of the holes and change colors. Pretty cool target!"
          }
        },
        "quote_HdC7L9": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Elevate your range experience!",
            "author": "M Simovic",
            "info": "",
            "date": "May 19th",
            "rate": 5,
            "quote": "DA Targets truly live up to the hype! The instant color feedback is a game changer – no more guessing where your shots landed."
          }
        },
        "quote_Lkmcjb": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A game changer!",
            "author": "C Burton",
            "info": "",
            "date": "May 19th",
            "rate": 5,
            "quote": "What a great product! My color changing targets are a game changer! I can see where I'm hitting without repainting gongs or stapling up new paper targets. Light and portable too, so I can set them up at any distance to practice different scenarios. After 1000 plus rounds, they are still holding up great! Thanks for a great product!"
          }
        },
        "quote_8NMFQd": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Lightweight & Easy To Carry",
            "author": "Chris R.",
            "info": "",
            "date": "May 19th",
            "rate": 5,
            "quote": "I use 6 of their knock down plates for Action Pistol practice. Their color change technology allows me to see exactly where I hit. With them being lighter it allows me to practice more since I don’t have to drag out a 500lb steel plate rack!"
          }
        },
        "quote_gpXtUe": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Lightweight reactive target.",
            "author": "Josh Welton",
            "info": "",
            "date": "April 28th",
            "rate": 5,
            "quote": "Nice reactive target! I've only used this DA Targets target so far with .22LR ammo, and the bullets pass through without taking any chunks out of the material. My only concern is that the base is a flexible material too and not metal as I had anticipated. I'm unsure how many hits the base can take before it becomes damaged. It may never become damaged from hits, but at this point I really don't know how it will react to getting shot as I've only used it for one range trip so far, and with a minimal caliber round.\n\nI mounted the base to a wooden 2x4, with the orange target hanging down. I didn't want to have to keep going out to the target to reset it, as I would have had I mounted it with the target at the top. With it hanging down, .22LR will go clean through and make the target move a little bit, allowing you to know you scored a hit. Time will tell as to how much abuse this target can take. Future range sessions will take place with larger calibers (all FMJ ammo).\n\nI'm not sure I like this any better though than a steel target. Steel targets if using the appropriate ammo for what the steel is rated for are a lifetime target. I guess the biggest advantage though to these Da Targets is their light weight. Most people could easily lift a rack of these targets, while they would be hard-pressed to lift a full rack of steels target."
          }
        },
        "quote_BTHEJi": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A fun addition!.",
            "author": "M Queen",
            "info": "",
            "date": "March 17th",
            "rate": 4,
            "quote": "This self-healing practice target seems like it'll be a lot of fun at the range. It says that it's appropriate for most common caliburs, with certain tip type exceptions. It feels like heavy-duty silicone, and it's about 1/2\" thick, and the target is a bright orange. It's got several holes to screw it to a board or bracket, and when you hit it, it'll fall backwards. This will be much more fun to use than just paper targets alone. The only downside is that it doesn't reset. We'll see about longevity with larger caliburs, though. I worry that it'll eventually start ripping apart."
          }
        },
        "quote_4NicmL": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Instant Shot Verification",
            "author": "Dave H.",
            "info": "",
            "date": "Feb 18th",
            "rate": 5,
            "quote": "You wonder why nobody thought of this sooner! These targets make your range day easier. Instant shot verification. \nLighter than lugging my steel around, simple to setup and NO PASTING cardboard. \nEveryone needs one of these. Now I need to get the plate rack🤘🏻"
          }
        }
      },
